## 2026-11-15 — Imapsync adoption gate preparation

- Completed T001: added root `.gitignore` rules for account `.secrets`, `.state`, and local probe output; verified with `git check-ignore -v` on representative paths.
- Completed T002: pinned public imapsync tag `imapsync-2.314` at commit `93654c6025ff7814f983ab74dd300f9bed9282d9` in ignored local storage; installed its missing Ubuntu Perl runtime modules; `./imapsync --version` returned `2.314` and `perl -c imapsync` returned `syntax OK`.
- Dependency review: NVD CVE-2023-34204 applies through imapsync 2.229, not pinned 2.314; newly installed Ubuntu packages had no pending upgrades. Details and installed versions are in `experiments/imapsync/probe.md`.
- Security finding: upstream `imapsync --tests` prints environment variables and later connects to external test servers. A second run with a scrubbed environment was stopped at the network-test phase. Do not run that command with secrets in the environment.
- Security finding: pinned imapsync 2.314 defaults to `SSL_VERIFY_NONE`. The plan and probe now require forced TLS and explicit certificate verification for both hosts, with invalid-certificate rejection in the gate.
- Completed T004: added a read-only IMAP probe and six offline tests for baseline UID filtering, exact UID batches, confirmed-copy filtering, and passfile permissions. `python3 -m unittest discover -s experiments/imapsync -p 'test_*.py' -v` passed (6 tests).
- T003 and T005–T007 remain pending disposable Yahoo and Gmail account credentials and live test fixtures. No live mail was copied.

## 2026-11-15 — Imapsync evaluation plan and implementation tasks

- Added `plan.md`, `research.md`, `data-model.md`, `contracts/cli.md`, `quickstart.md`, and `tasks.md` under `specs/0/0.001-imap-mail-sync/`.
- Selected imapsync as a conditional transfer-engine candidate, with a blocking disposable Yahoo-to-Gmail proof of concept before production transfer implementation. The gate covers first-activation baselines, duplicate identity, repeat runs, destination deletion behavior, flag stability, attachments, uncertain APPEND recovery, and source outage isolation.
- Planned a Python 3.12 CLI wrapper, versioned SQLite state, per-source imapsync caches, and a five-minute systemd user timer if the candidate passes. A no-go result requires revising the plan and tasks for direct IMAP transfer.
- Recorded the RFC 9051 UID-range edge case: a bare `UID n:*` can include an old last message when `n` exceeds all assigned UIDs, so the wrapper must enumerate and filter explicit eligible UIDs.
- Validation: reviewed task ordering and spec coverage; no live mail was copied because disposable provider credentials are not available in the repository. No application code or dependencies were added in this planning step.

